mali-valhall-g610 (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship a udev rule opening /dev/dma_heap/{system,system-uncached} to the
    render group and the active seat user. libmali allocates from these heaps;
    with the default root-only 0600 nodes its gbm_create_device() fails with
    ENOENT and GNOME Shell/mutter cannot start.
  * Pass WQ_PERCPU to the six implicitly per-CPU workqueues, silencing the
    alloc_workqueue() WARN on 6.17+ kernels (defined as 0 on older kernels).

 -- Ivan Podogov <ginkage.uk@gmail.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:59:00 +0100

mali-valhall-g610 (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging of the Rockchip Mali-Valhall (CSF) DKMS module.
  * Builds valhall_kbase.ko (Mali-G610, platform rk, ARM DDK g29p1) on mainline
    ARM64 kernels via DKMS, installed to /usr/src/mali-valhall-g610-g29p1.
  * Ships the rockchip-drm render-node, system-uncached dma-heap, and optional
    GPU page-migration kernel patches under kernel-patches/ (see README.md).

 -- Ivan Podogov <ginkage.uk@gmail.com>  Tue, 30 Jun 2026 16:08:22 +0100
